From 83bfc9b5c2fb464588555d288359f59efe9bb219 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 12:49:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 42/75] wm: force ARC container task origin to (0,0) regardless
 of bounds source
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A dialog/modal ARC task (e.g. SystemUI's WifiDebuggingActivity) rendered
with the wrong on-screen location and an input offset (taps landed off the
card; VRI logged "updatePointerIcon ... position out of bounds"). Root cause:
the task's WMS frame had a non-zero origin (160,0) instead of the (0,0,W,H)
required in ARC container mode, where HWC/Wayland (Chrome) owns the on-screen
position and the InputDispatcher frame must match the task-local coords SF
emits.

LaunchParamsUtil.centerBounds already forces (0,0,W,H) for freshly-centered
windows (the AOSP-13 port of patch 0027 / the IS_CONTAINER branch), but two
paths bypass it:
  - bounds RESTORED from LaunchParamsPersister (currentParams.mBounds, the
    "inherit-bounds" branch in STEP 2.2), and
  - the freeform conflict-avoidance cascade (adjustBoundsToAvoidConflict...).
A normal app gets its origin re-zeroed by Chrome's geometry reposition, but a
dialog/modal task receives no such reposition, so the bad origin sticks AND is
re-persisted — a self-perpetuating persist->restore->re-save loop. (Confirmed
on device: deleting the stale launch_params file made the next launch compute
(0,0) and the "position out of bounds" spam stopped.)

Force the origin to (0,0) for every container task at the end of calculate(),
preserving the resolved size, regardless of how the bounds were derived. This
also heals already-persisted bad origins on the next launch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I82395ad46487bf48465d04e3df54dedd7d2b665f
---
 .../server/wm/TaskLaunchParamsModifier.java   | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/TaskLaunchParamsModifier.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/TaskLaunchParamsModifier.java
index dcd830da1b8b..65aa9083f770 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/TaskLaunchParamsModifier.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/TaskLaunchParamsModifier.java
@@ -416,6 +416,28 @@ class TaskLaunchParamsModifier implements LaunchParamsModifier {
             applyArcAspectRatio(root, display, outParams);
         }
 
+        // fydroid-rt: In ARC container mode the task's on-screen position is
+        // owned by HWC/Wayland (Chrome), never by Android WM — the WMS frame
+        // must stay at origin (0,0) so the InputDispatcher frame matches the
+        // task-local coords SF emits (see the IS_CONTAINER branch in
+        // LaunchParamsUtil.centerBounds). centerBounds enforces this only for
+        // freshly-centered windows; bounds RESTORED from LaunchParamsPersister
+        // (currentParams.mBounds — the "inherit-bounds" path above) or shifted
+        // by the freeform conflict-avoidance cascade bypass it and can carry a
+        // non-zero origin. For a dialog/modal task that origin never gets
+        // corrected (the modal path receives no Chrome geometry reposition), so
+        // the input frame ends up offset from the centered card the compositor
+        // draws — taps land off-card and VRI logs "updatePointerIcon ... position
+        // out of bounds". Worse, the bad origin is then re-persisted, so it
+        // self-perpetuates across launches. Force the origin to (0,0) for every
+        // container task, preserving the resolved size, regardless of how the
+        // bounds were derived.
+        if (android.os.Build.IS_CONTAINER && !outParams.mBounds.isEmpty()
+                && (outParams.mBounds.left != 0 || outParams.mBounds.top != 0)) {
+            if (DEBUG) appendLog("container-zero-origin: was=" + outParams.mBounds);
+            outParams.mBounds.offsetTo(0, 0);
+        }
+
         return RESULT_CONTINUE;
     }
 
